+// Max completed 3 ms DMA blocks delivered per tick. Draining several at once catches up
+// backlog from a long frame without letting a large stall spiral into an unbounded loop.
+constexpr int kMaxBlocksPerTick = 32;
+
+// perf.cfg `ax_tick_yield_busy` (default 0 since b59 hardware run): when one tick owes several audio blocks, the next
+// block used to join the mix the previous block had dispatched a few microseconds earlier, so
+// the guest waited out (and helped with) every mix in the burst: JoinMix was 1.5% of the b56
+// race guest thread. Leaving the owed time in the accumulator instead lets the woken sound
+// thread run while the mix worker finishes; the next scheduler pass takes the next block. That
+// is also the hardware order (DMA interrupt, sound thread, next DMA interrupt). Every block is
+// still delivered: nothing is dropped, only the burst is spread over the following passes.
+// Measured cost (b59 race): nw4r's sound thread queue holds 4 messages and the AX callback posts
+// with OS_MESSAGE_NOBLOCK, so the eager burst dropped sound-thread updates beyond the queue; the
+// interleaving delivered every one and roughly doubled sound-thread work (+2.4 ms/frame). Off by
+// default; kept for experiments.
+// Beyond this backlog the tick drains as before (joining each mix), so a caller that will not
+// poll again soon can never leave audio starving.
+constexpr int kYieldMaxOwedBlocks = 16;
+
+bool AxTickYieldWhenMixBusy()
+{
+    static const bool enabled = kartpad_opt != nullptr && kartpad_opt("ax_tick_yield_busy", 0) != 0;
+    return enabled;
+}
